# This portfolio is a fully static Vite build.
#
# It needs NO environment variables and no server. All content lives in
# src/lib/data.ts, the resume is a static file in public/resume, and the GitHub
# card reads GitHub live from the browser (public contribution calendar plus the
# public repository list), falling back to src/lib/github-contributions.ts only
# when those requests fail.
#
# Nothing here should be committed with real values. If a form or API key is
# added later, put it in `.env` locally (copy this file) and in
# Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables for the deployment, never in source.
#
# Optional, and not needed for Vercel. Point this at a deployment that serves its
# own JSON feed of GitHub activity (the Cloudflare Worker in sites/worker.js
# answers /api/github, cached at the edge). When set, that feed is preferred over
# the direct public fetch; when unset, the browser reads GitHub directly.
# VITE_GITHUB_ENDPOINT=/api/github
